# rp2350_zero

A Waveshare RP2350-Zero, the mini board: an RP2350A with 4MB of flash by
Waveshare's description and the SDK's header, on the RP2040-Zero's 23.5 by
18 mm board with a USB-C socket on the native port and a WS2812B RGB LED on
GP16.

It derives from pico2-arm because that is what it is: the same RP2350A the
Pico SDK configures as pico2. As with rp2040_zero, the SDK's
waveshare_rp2350_zero header is outside the bridge's vendor vocabulary, so the
board derives and the board table corrects. The chip, the SDK, and the ABI
come from pico2-arm.

It binds platform.zero.led, which drives the WS2812B on GP16 as mm.led
through mm.led.ws2812b and mm.mcu pulse instance zero.

The 23-pin header carries GP0 to GP15 and GP26 to GP29, with 3V3, GND, and
VBUS; ten castellated pads carry GP17 to GP25. GP16 drives the WS2812B and is
not brought out. Unlike the RP2040-Zero, it has a three-pin SWD footprint, J2,
on the chip's own SWDIO and SWCLK. Its 3V3 comes from an ME6217 linear
regulator rather than a Pico 2's switcher, so pico2's PICO_SMPS_MODE_PIN,
GP23, is a free pad here; nothing in the bridge drives it.

The board table replaces the same pico2 default it replaces for rp2040_zero:
GP25 is a free pad and the WS2812B is the only LED, so the board reports no
LED. UART0 on GP0 and GP1 stands, and GP26 and GP27 and GP8 and GP9 being free
header pins, the board has the second I2C and second UART wirings. ADC_AVDD is
the 3V3 rail, so the ADC reference is 3300 mV.

Every pin above was read from Waveshare's schematic, RP2350_Zero.pdf. Its
flash symbol is labelled W25Q16, a 2MB part, against the 4MB the product page
and the SDK state; pico2-arm assumes 4MB, so an image past 2MB is the one that
would find out. None of it is qualified on hardware.

https://www.waveshare.com/wiki/RP2350-Zero
